From c158f50722808ababe6e913e32bc63e37f1baa77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 09:34:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 412: who teaches the pick - the reach verb never had
 cross-entropy

Found in the source: loss_for reads OBJECTIVE only on the lookup path, and a
reach question is handed to reach_loss two lines earlier. Every reach number in
this project was trained by the payoff term - one scalar per question - and
cross-entropy was never available on that verb at all.

That is an information rate, not a philosophy: the payoff carries what one
settled world was worth, while -log p(truth) moves the truth up and every rival
down in proportion to what each took. The two have never been raced on the same
worlds, tape and offer.

--pick-teacher stage keeps today bit for bit and is the default. `reward` and
`ce` are the paired arms: identical but for the teacher, both with the router's
branch value detached, so the teacher is the only difference. CE targets REFUSE
where the offer does not hold the truth, which is what keeps the two arms on the
same population - without it CE would train on an eighth of the questions and the
comparison would be of coverage. pick_target reports that share and is the void
check.

391's checker property 6 was edited rather than worked around: the return is now
two lines so the pick term sits beside the move term; the property and its
mutation are unchanged in meaning.

_check412_pick.py: seven properties, six mutation-verified.

